#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# crossing_count

#% text
# `crossing_count(curve, p)` gives the least number of times a ray from `p` crosses the closed curve, over all directions of the ray; a point on the curve adds 1.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
crossing_count([[0, 0], [2, 0], [2, 2], [0, 2]], [1, 1])
#% output
#= 1

